# .env.example — structure only, no real values.
#
# hfss-agent is a zero-egress, local-only tool (see CLAUDE.md: "Zero
# egress" hard rule). It makes no outbound network calls, so nothing in
# this file is required to run the package today.
#
# If a real secret is ever needed in the future (e.g. a PyPI publish
# token for releasing this package), it belongs in GitHub Actions
# repository secrets — never in a committed file, never in a local .env
# that gets accidentally staged. This file exists so the convention is
# documented before it's needed, not because anything currently reads it.
